Welcome to the tapbridge installer.

tapbridge lets you use your Android phone as your Mac smart-card reader: tap your FIDO/PIV security key on the phone, and the Mac sees it as a locally attached reader.

This install adds:

\b /usr/local/libexec/SmartCardServices/drivers/tapbridge.bundle\b0  - the PC/SC reader driver (IFDHandler) that bridges to the daemon

\b /usr/local/bin/tapbridge\b0  - the tapbridge daemon (tray app)

You will be asked for an administrator password because the reader driver lives in a system directory.

Click Continue to begin.
